{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792231720,"nonce":"W+sDcqi4wctEtAr66w/pnoM4afg=","title":"binarytrees: fuse tree build + fold like Ash's tree_fusion (drop the per-iteration allocations)","message":"Ash's binarytrees win is build/fold fusion (deforestation), not an allocator. A call that builds a recursive tree, immediately followed by a recursive fold over it, is replaced by one scalar recursive helper that never allocates. Ash's bench (crates/ash/test/tests/BenchBinaryTrees.hx) is identical to compiler/benchmarks/src/binarytrees.hx; there allocation went 900 MiB -\u003e 4 MiB (only the long-lived tree remains), NUC median 334.2 -\u003e 128.2 ms.\n\nAsh sources (read-only reference):\n- analysis: crates/air/src/v2/tree_fusion.rs (Checker::execute, pair, branch, analyze_pair, survey; TreeModule contract, Limits)\n- rewrite: crates/air/src/v2/tree_fusion/fuse.rs (build_helper, rewrite_caller)\n- driver: crates/ash/src/tree_fusion.rs (refuses hosted modules, external natives, drop/tail hooks, reload)\n- docs: docs/debugging.md:201-244, :303-369; bench/README.md:86-141, :326-397\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Survey callers on pre-inlining IR. Look for a call returning a class with a self-typed field (the producer), followed by a call taking that root as its only argument (the consumer). Between them only copies and null checks are allowed, and the root has no other use, alias escape, phi or handler. The long-lived tree fails this, so it is kept.\n2. Prove the pair by symbolically executing both arms of the `depth \u003e 0` guard.\n   - Producer: recursion only passes `depth-1`, and the root is one fresh allocation. Every field is set exactly once to an int, a fresh child or null, and leaves have null children.\n   - Consumer: reads only root fields, and recurses once on each fresh child.\n   - Whitelist: integer Add/Sub/Mul/And/Or/Xor/Neg (wrapping). No loops, mutation, floats, division or unknown calls.\n3. Emit a helper `(scalar args) -\u003e i32`, replace the consumer call with it and drop the producer call. DCE then removes the allocation. On any failure the whole transaction is dropped.\n4. Budgets: 256 ops per body, 16,384 proof steps, 64 sites, 32 helpers.\n\nRayzor mapping:\n- New module pass compiler/src/ir/tree_fusion.rs in PassManager::for_level (O2/O3).\n- Place it after UnreachableBlockElimination and BEFORE the first InsertFreePass (free_deep would add a root use) and BEFORE InliningPass (producer and consumer must still be separate CallDirects).\n- Allocators to recognise as the fresh root: classify_func in insert_free.rs.\n- Extra preconditions: the consumer method must resolve statically (no override; devirtualization runs later). No Reflect/Type identity use of the class. The tiered backend's cached MIR must be the fused one.\n\nCurrent rayzor: size-class object pool (runtime/src/object_pool.rs) plus owned-field deep free; all ~29.6M nodes are still allocated and freed. CI 2026-10-16 x86: rayzor-tiered 328 ms vs hxcpp 397 ms (already ahead, but this is the lever for a large margin, cold and warm).","files":null}]}